{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_fault_f59_3_f59_3", "label": "Fault F59.3 \u2014 the c=1e6 walk was run at c = 137.035999", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F59.3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f59_3_cinf_patch", "label": "cinf.py default-argument rebinding patch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F59.3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The patch rebinds __defaults__ on three kernel functions, but HFSR.__init__ carries its own c=C0 bound at import and passes c POSITIONALLY, so the patched default is unreachable. The probe call site is the one place that does use the default \u2014 the instrument was validated on a path the physics never takes."}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f59_3_immunity_theorem", "label": "The 94/107 immunity theorem (combinatorial, c-independent)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F59.3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f59_3_can_fail_the_fix", "label": "A patch that changes nothing is the fault, not the fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F59.3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The corrected rebinding must be asserted where c is actually read (t7c_hfsr.C0, HFSR.__init__.__defaults__, hfc2.C0) and must be shown to MOVE Z=79's D_ent before any walk is trusted \u2014 the kernel shifts Z=79's 1s by 314.08 Ha when c reaches it, so a zero shift proves the patch never arrived."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_fault_f59_3_f59_3", "target": "recovered_fault_f59_3_cinf_patch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F59.3.md